 "final_text": "Submitted. Summary of the answer sent to Robin:\n\n| Week | Window (Mon\u2013Sun) | Net |\n|---|---|---|\n| Week 1 | Aug 10\u201316, 2026 | $0 |\n| Week 2 | Aug 17\u201323, 2026 | $0 |\n| Week 3 | Aug 24\u201330, 2026 | $0 |\n| Week 4 | Aug 31\u2013Sep 6, 2026 | $0 |\n| **4-week total** | | **$0** |\n\n**Why it's flat:** Applying TRS-SOP-004 literally, none of CESP's open AR (3 invoices, due Mar 5/12/18/2026), open AP (3 invoices, due Mar 4/11/25/2026), or scheduled payroll fundings (Feb 27, Mar 13, Mar 27/2026) fall inside the Aug 10\u2013Sep 6, 2026 window \u2014 they're all past due relative to today and, per the SOP's explicit rule, get ignored rather than dumped into week 1 or assumed to recur. CESP's ledgers (AR/AP subledgers, fiscal periods, bank balance snapshot) are all populated only through March 2026, so there's simply nothing booked yet against the requested window.\n\nThis is worth flagging to Robin before Thursday's board call \u2014 a genuine $0 four-week forecast almost certainly means CESP's forward AR/AP/payroll data hasn't been loaded into the ERP for the period in question, not that cash flow is actually flat. Worth a quick check with whoever owns CESP's books before presenting this number.",
